supralinux-drivers (1.0.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Delegate driver changes to Ubuntu's ubuntu-drivers install through
    pkexec, instead of building package IDs for PackageKit. That follows the
    Ubuntu kernel meta package, installs the signed prebuilt modules and runs
    the NVIDIA hooks. Package index refresh uses apt-get update.
  * Remove the manual NVIDIA/kernel package selection introduced in 1.0.6.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300

supralinux-drivers (1.0.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install the prebuilt linux-modules-nvidia package for the running kernel
    instead of the generic meta package. The meta can point to a newer kernel
    ABI whose linux-modules package is not available, which made the NVIDIA
    install fail with unmet dependencies. If no prebuilt package exists, add
    the matching kernel headers so DKMS can build the driver.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0300

